00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:08.580
than trying to look like one of the faces made of rock

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.020
from that 90s kids show.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.300
Yeah. Oh, Legends of the Hidden Temple?

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.780
Yeah. That's what I was thinking of,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:16.680
but I couldn't figure it out.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.660
Yeah, all that from Legends of the Hidden Temple. Also, if Dark didn't take on the embodiment of a face, though,

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.140
it'd be really hard to have like a final boss in this game.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.240
It would just be, imagine that reveal at the end,

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.320
I'm everywhere.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.860
And then you have to shoot all over the screen.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.980
I mean the cartridge. The cartridge itself is the end.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.640
Completely unrealistic.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.860
But just, you know, now two young warriors,

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.840
they're given the wings of love and courage

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.400
by none other than the god of war himself, Ares.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.300
So I question if it's the real Ares

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.760
because in the manual, Ares is in quotation marks.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.820
Which makes me think it's like Ares,

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.300
like with air quotes around it.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.760
God of war gave two young men.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.320
I mean, these aren't even real angels.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.000
Right. It's all over the place.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.340
This has no common theme at all.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.880
Can I just, I mean, I could just read the whole story

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:04.800
because it's pretty short here.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.160
I don't know. You've been given permission.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.140
I'd like to read the whole story

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.300
because I love the ending of it.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.760
Ares, god of war, gave two young men courage

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.140
and wings of love to save the world from extinction.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.020
Ares entrusted them with the survival

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.600
of the future of the human race.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.280
Time is of essence.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.980
Take wings. Legendary wings.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.820
Is that like his like James Bond,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.440
like drop the mic kind of like,

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:31.460
he's trying to be like epic?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.640
It sounds like a commercial

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.840
for like a place that does chicken wings.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.760
Yeah. Legendary wings.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.660
Also like for the god of war

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.760
to be talking like that.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.520
Right. I expected something a lot more epic.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.140
But also he wasn't talking in this whole story

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:46.420
until the last two sentences

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.000
where suddenly we're like coming off,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:49.880
coming from his voice.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:50.860
Take wings. I don't know.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:54.300
Legendary wings. Yeah, there's no sense of tense

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.820
or anything like that in these older games.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.320
You get whatever you get

00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.260
and you don't get upset.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.320
Exactly. Aww.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.240
Yeah. I'm just gonna,

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.680
rather than do this whole thing

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:04.840
where we talk about controls

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.120
and we talk about levels

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.340
and layouts and stuff like that.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:08.320
Just end now.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.740
Instead of talking about this game at all.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.460
I'm gonna get right into the meat and potatoes

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.860
of what makes this a different kind of shmup

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.180
from the ones we played before.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.400
And I think it's something

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.440
that a game like Gradius needed,

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.120
which is really cool.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.620
And that is that your power-ups

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.800
are your health bars.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.600
So when you are on like stage one power-up,

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.000
you technically can take a single hit.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.080
And when you're on stage three,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.660
you can take three hits

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.660
or four total hits before you die.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.640
and you won't reach a,

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.740
you won't use another life.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.980
Right. It's almost like Mario rules a little bit

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:46.900
where you have the mushroom.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.400
Yeah, where that's like the power-up mushroom.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:52.240
Yeah. And I thought that was really a great solve

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:56.020
into a game that usually gives you one hit

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.060
and you're dead. What did you guys think about that?

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.060
I loved it. I mean, I did feel like,

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.780
at first I was frustrated

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:02.920
as I usually am with shmups

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.000
because whenever I get hit by anything,

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.620
I'm not a big shmup fan anyways.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.760
So having that ability

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.920
to kind of cushion your experience

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.760
and be able to keep going

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.320
after getting hit or making a mistake

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.640
was helpful. Yeah, it's definitely

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.320
sort of a positive feedback loop.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:20.360
Like if you do well,

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.380
you're going to do better.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.460
If you do poorly,

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.560
you're going to do worse.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.800
I'm of two minds on that,

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.880
on that like philosophy of difficulty.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:34.600
I think that there should be a balance

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.320
that maybe you have more power-ups

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.660
and you can take more hits,

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:40.880
but maybe now there's going to be

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.380
a bit more enemies to counter that.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.480
But I mean, it definitely did provide a power fantasy.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.320
When I was at the full health,

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.980
I felt like a human with angel wings on my back.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.580
Wings of love and courage.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.920
No, it's just courage

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.020
and then wings of love.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.920
And I agree with the balance thing,

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.600
but I'm not sure I would love having

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.720
when I get more power-ups,

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.520
there's more enemies because then it makes my power-ups

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.520
feel kind of...

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.320
That's why there are different thought processes.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.400
There are different ways to go about difficulty.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.940
Right, right. Well, I think the biggest thing here though

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.800
is the way the power-ups work

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.800
is that they're given throughout the stage

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.400
as you defeat enemies and stuff like that.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:22.540
So it's something you must collect.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.080
It really is a great way

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.380
when as you're leveling up to,

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.440
like let's say you're on stage three

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.900
of your power-ups, it's a great way to make it through

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.740
the normal part of the stage.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.840
However, once you get to the boss-like character,

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.680
it reveals that it pretty much wanted you

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.860
to have all those power-ups to begin with

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.520
because if you take three hits from,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.680
let's say even the first boss, the dragon,

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.020
if you take three hits from him

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.180
and now you're back to your regular power-up,

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.760
you cannot collect any additional power-ups,

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.780
which I think is a bit of a mistake here.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:55.800
But more importantly,

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.400
the game expected you to either know

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.640
that you should have like your power-ups

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.640
at all times and not take hits

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.280
or it expected you to know that like,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.280
oh, in shmups, you know,

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.300
you just got to shoot things

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.240
over and over and over again

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.320
because that dragon on level one

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.640
without any power-ups

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.420
will take approximately 50 to 75 hits

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.420
to the face.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.760
Like not even to its, its body doesn't count.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.640
So you have to be pretty accurate with that too.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.680
And that's just the first level of the boss.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.160
So I think the game made the mistake

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:29.100
not in rewarding good players,

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.500
but in the fact that it really punished you.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:32.560
Yeah, it punishes you

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.500
if you don't have the, you know,

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.920
the optimal amount of power-ups.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.960
Or even some level of power-up.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.160
And that's sort of what I meant

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.820
because, well, yeah,

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.500
maybe we shouldn't add enemies

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:46.540
when you get better,

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.380
but there has to be some kind of aid

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.340
for when you have the pea shooter

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.460
and you will die if you get touched by anything.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.460
Right. Especially because you can't even,

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.880
I mean, you can't even, sometimes I can't even tell

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.580
if I'm hitting anything when I have the pea shooter.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.160
Like that's really frustrating too

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:00.960
because then I don't even know

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.420
if it's worth me shooting at this thing

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.400
if I just go around it,

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.340
which brings up other problems,

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.220
which I'm sure we'll get into later.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:10.860
. .

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.720
. .

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:35.260
. . . Thank you.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:04.200
So we mentioned the power-ups give you health, but we didn't really talk about the power-ups themselves.

